\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. The Maker of the sun and moon,
\par The Maker of our earth,
\par Lo, late in time, a fairer boon,
\par Himself is brought to birth.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. How blest was all creation then,
\par When God so gave increase;
\par And Christ, to heal the hearts of men,
\par Brought righteousness and peace.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. No star in all the heights of heaven
\par But burned to see Him go;
\par Yet unto earth alone was given
\par His human form to know
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. His human form, by man denied,
\par Took death for human sin;
\par His endless love, through faith descried,
\par Still lives the world to win.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. O perfect Love, outpassing sight
\par O light beyond our ken,
\par Come down through all the world to-night,
\par And heal the hearts of  men!
\par                                Amen.
\par \f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2 
\par }

